meta {
  name: Bulk create (partial success)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/transactions/bulk
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "transactions": [
      {
        "accountId": "acc_chequing",
        "date": "{{today}}",
        "amount": -1250,
        "description": "Coffee",
        "categoryId": "cat_coffee"
      },
      {
        "accountId": "acc_chequing",
        "date": "{{today}}",
        "amount": -12.5,
        "description": "This row fails: amount is not minor units"
      },
      {
        "accountId": "acc_cash",
        "date": "{{today}}",
        "amount": 2000,
        "description": "Cash found in a coat"
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Max 1000 rows. **Partial success is the point:**
  
  | status | |
  |---|---|
  | `201` | all created |
  | `207` | some created — `errors[]` carries the index and reason for each failure |
  | `422` | none created |
  
  As written this returns `207`: rows 0 and 2 are created, row 1 comes back in
  `errors[]` with its index. A client that ignores `207` silently loses data.
}
